6. What is StringBuilder?
StringBuilder is a mutable sequence of characters.

Key Characteristics:
Mutable((can be changed)
Not thread-safe
Faster than StringBuffer
Introduced in Java 5
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");

Interview one-liner
“Use StringBuilder when you need fast, mutable strings in single-threaded scenarios.”

7. StringBuilder Example
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");
        sb.append(" Spring");
        sb.append(" Boot");

        System.out.println(sb);
    }
}

Output
Java Spring Boot

👉 Same object is modified → better performance

8. StringBuilder Important Methods
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");
| Method                 | Result              |
| ---------------------- | ------------------- |
| `sb.append(" Spring")` | Java Spring         |
| `sb.insert(4," Core")` | Java Core           |
| `sb.delete(4,9)`       | Java                |
| `sb.reverse()`         | avaJ                |
| `sb.capacity()`        | default 16 + length |

