9. What is StringBuffer?

StringBuffer is similar to StringBuilder but thread-safe.

Key Characteristics:
Mutable
Thread-safe (synchronized)
Slower than StringBuilder
Introduced in Java 1.0

StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer("Java");

Interview one-liner
“StringBuffer is thread-safe but slower due to synchronization.”

10. StringBuffer Example
public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer("Java");
        sb.append(" Spring");

        System.out.println(sb);
    }
}

Output
Java Spring

11. String vs StringBuilder vs StringBuffer (🔥 MOST IMPORTANT)
| Feature     | String      | StringBuilder | StringBuffer |
| ----------- | ----------- | ------------- | ------------ |
| Mutability  | ❌ Immutable | ✅ Mutable     | ✅ Mutable    |
| Thread-safe | ✅           | ❌             | ✅            |
| Performance | Slow        | Fastest       | Slower       |
| Memory      | SCP         | Heap          | Heap         |
| Use case    | Constants   | Single-thread | Multi-thread |

12. Performance Comparison (Interview Favorite 🔥)
long start = System.currentTimeMillis();

String s = "Java";
for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
    s = s + "a";
}

long end = System.currentTimeMillis();
System.out.println(end - start);


👉 Very slow due to multiple object creation

StringBuilder (Fast)
StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder("Java");
for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
    sb.append("a");
}

✔ Reuses same object
✔ Much faster

13. Why String is Immutable? (🔥 Very Common Question)
Security (ClassLoader, DB URLs)
Thread safety
Caching in SCP
HashCode consistency (used in HashMap)

14. Strings as HashMap Keys (Very Important)
Map<String, String> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("key", "value");


👉 Immutability ensures:
HashCode doesn’t change
Data integrity in collections

15. StringBuilder vs StringBuffer – When to Use?
| Scenario        | Choice        |
| --------------- | ------------- |
| Single thread   | StringBuilder |
| Multi thread    | StringBuffer  |
| Constants       | String        |
| Logging / loops | StringBuilder |

17. Common Tricky Interview Questions (4+ Years)
Q1. Is String thread-safe?
✅ Yes (immutable)

Q2. Does StringBuilder override equals()?
❌ No (uses Object.equals → reference comparison)

Q3. Can StringBuffer and StringBuilder store null?
❌ No (append(null) adds "null" string)

Q4. Why StringBuilder is faster than String?
Because it does not create new objects
